      "node_id": "kg_doc_3",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Galina Valentinovna Chistyakova (Russian: Галина Валентиновна Чистякова , Slovak: \"Galina Čisťaková\" ; born 26 July 1962) is a retired athlete who represented the Soviet Union and later Slovakia. She is the current world record holder in the long jump, jumping 7.52 metres on 11 June 1988. She is the 1988 Olympic bronze medallist and the 1989 World Indoor champion. She is also a former world record holder (pre IAAF) in the triple jump with 14.52 metres in 1989.",
